<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helena Kantakouzene</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. after 1394</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helena Kantakouzene was a Byzantine noblewoman, granddaughter of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-kantakouzenos">John VI Kantakouzenos</a>, who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-fadrique">Louis Fadrique</a>, Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amfissa">Salona</a>. After his death in 1382 she governed the county for their daughter Maria. In 1394 she surrendered Salona to the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a>, and her daughter was taken into his harem.</p></div>
